      "id": "W1-hashrow",
      "outputs": ["q2_dim_customer_checksum"],
      "columns": ["HASH_SUM"],
      "change": "SUM(HASHROW(CUSTOMER_ID, FIRST_NAME, LAST_NAME, CUSTOMER_SEGMENT)) replaced by the sum of the first 64 bits of SHA-256 over a canonical string, computed identically in the derived reference and the Snowflake port.",
      "reason": "HASHROW is Teradata's AMP row-distribution hash (BYTE(4)); it has no Snowflake equivalent and its values cannot be reproduced on another engine. The replacement is case- and whitespace-preserving, so it is stricter than HASHROW on NOT CASESPECIFIC columns.",
